  "validity_reason": "Both answers accurately reflect the source: -32002 for resource-not-found, -32603 for internal errors, the example shows an error object with code -32002, message, and data.uri, and the source mandates URI validation.",
  "selected_answerer": "both"
}

{
  "final_answer_text": "If the client adds or removes filesystem roots but does not call rootsListChangedNotification, the server will not receive notifications of those changes and therefore will not have an up-to-date understanding of which filesystem roots (directories and files) it may access. That stale view can lead to incorrect or unsafe behavior, so the client must call rootsListChangedNotification so the server can obtain the current roots list.",
  "final_source_quote": "The roots capability allows servers to:

* Request the list of accessible filesystem roots
* Receive notifications when the roots list changes
* Understand which directories and files they have access to

// Add a root dynamically
client.addRoot(new Root("file:///path", "description"));

// Remove a root
client.removeRoot("file:///path");

// Notify server of roots changes
client.rootsListChangedNotification();",
  "validity": "valid",
  "validity_reason": "The source explicitly states servers can receive notifications of roots list changes and understand which directories/files they may access; lacking the notification means the server won't learn updates and thus can have a stale, incorrect view.",
  "selected_answerer": "both"
}

{
  "final_answer_text": "If you register the wrong customizer type (sync vs async), the MCP transport will not use your customizer and your request modifications will not be applied. The customizer type must match the MCP client type because you must implement the corresponding interface (McpSyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer or McpAsyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer) that the transport expects.",
  "final_source_quote": "To dynamically modify HTTP request before they are issued, implement either `McpSyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer` or `McpAsyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer`.
Choose the request customizer matching the MCP Client type, sync or async.

// Sync
class MyRequestCustomizer implements McpSyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer { ... }

// Async
class MyAsyncRequestCustomizer implements McpAsyncHttpClientRequestCustomizer { ... }",
